            <ArticleTitle>Microwave-assisted synthesis of hydroxyl-containing isoquinolines by metal-free radical cyclization of vinyl isocyanides with alcohols.</ArticleTitle>
            <Pagination>
                <MedlinePgn>10044-10052</MedlinePgn>
            </Pagination>
            <ELocationID EIdType="doi" ValidYN="Y">10.1039/c7ob02221b</ELocationID>
            <Abstract>
                <AbstractText>A convenient microwave-assisted protocol for the synthesis of hydroxyl-containing isoquinolines from a metal-free radical cyclization reaction of vinyl isonitriles with alcohols was developed with moderate-to-excellent yields. Vinyl isonitriles are coupled with alkyl radicals through direct catalytic functionalization of the α sp3 C-H bond of alcohols. The methodology demonstrates a broad substrate scope, shows excellent functional group tolerance, is highly atom-economical and highly efficient, thus enabling the preparation of diverse potentially valuable hydroxyl-containing isoquinolines.</AbstractText>
            </Abstract>
